---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pulse Propulsion" description="How to approach light speed using Temporal Decoupling.">
  <article class="container" style="padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>Temporal Pulse Propulsion</h1>
    <p class="lead">Standard physics says the energy required to reach light speed is infinite. <strong>Temporal Decoupling</strong> explains why: Light speed is not just a velocity; it is the boundary between our Timeline and the Timeless Sea (TSC). Crossing it requires infinite energy to overcome the temporal pressure gradient.</p>

    <!-- Interactive Simulation -->
    <div style="background: #020617; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 16px; margin: 2rem 0; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #1e293b;">
      <canvas id="pulseCanvas" width="800" height="400" style="display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 800px; height: 400px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 0 auto;"></canvas>
      
      <div style="margin-top: 1rem; display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <button id="btnStandard" style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid #334155; background: #1e293b; color: #fff;">Standard Drive</button>
        <button id="btnPulse" style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; background: #2563EB; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 4px;">Pulse Drive (Theory)</button>
        <button id="btnReset" style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid #334155; background: #1e293b; color: #fff;">Reset</button>
      </div>
      
      <p id="statusText" style="color: #94a3b8; margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; min-height: 1.5em; padding: 0 1rem;">Select a drive mode to visualize temporal pressure.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>The Mechanic: Temporal Pressure & The Boundary</h2>
    <p>In this model, acceleration does not just increase speed; it increases <strong>Temporal Pressure</strong>. As the ship pushes against the flowline, it creates a "bulge" of resistance (visualized as the darkening blue gradient).</p>
    
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The Gradient Bulge:</strong> Mass creates drag on the timeline. Acceleration intensifies this drag, compressing the temporal field around the ship. The darker the blue, the higher the energy cost to maintain thrust.</li>
      <li><strong>Pulse Coasting:</strong> By stopping acceleration, the ship decouples from the active push. The temporal pressure dissipates (gradient fades), allowing the ship to conserve energy while maintaining momentum through space.</li>
      <li><strong>The Light Speed Barrier:</strong> Represented by the black vertical bar. As velocity approaches <em>c</em>, the temporal pressure becomes infinite. To cross this barrier would require leaving our timeline entirely, entering the TSC where the momentum difference could dismantle physical matter.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Why Earth Launch Requires So Much Power</h3>
    <p>This visualization also explains planetary launch. The Earth itself has a massive temporal bulge (gravity). To leave Earth, a ship must overcome both its own temporal drag AND the Earth's deep temporal well. The combined gradients create an immense energy threshold just to reach orbit.</p>
  </article>

  <script is:inline>
    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
    } else {
      init();
    }

    function init() {
      const canvas = document.getElementById('pulseCanvas');
      if (!canvas) return;
      const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
      const btnStandard = document.getElementById('btnStandard');
      const btnPulse = document.getElementById('btnPulse');
      const btnReset = document.getElementById('btnReset');
      const statusText = document.getElementById('statusText');

      let animationId;
      let mode = 'none';
      let velocity = 0;
      let pressure = 0; // 0 to 1 (represents gradient darkness)
      let distance = 0; // Simulated distance for stars
      let energy = 100;
      
      // Starfield
      const stars = [];
      const numStars = 150;
      for(let i=0; i<numStars; i++) {
        stars.push({
          x: Math.random() * 800,
          y: Math.random() * 400,
          size: Math.random() * 2 + 0.5,
          speed: Math.random() * 0.5 + 0.1
        });
      }

      // Tuning
      const MAX_SPEED = 5.0;
      const BARRIER_POS = 700; // X position of the black bar

      function resizeCanvas() {
        const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
        const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
        canvas.width = rect.width * dpr;
        canvas.height = rect.height * dpr;
        ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);
        canvas.logicalWidth = rect.width;
        canvas.logicalHeight = rect.height;
      }

      function draw() {
        const w = canvas.logicalWidth || 800;
        const h = canvas.logicalHeight || 400;
        
        // 1. Background Gradient (Temporal Pressure)
        // Interpolate color based on pressure
        // Low pressure: Light Blue (#3b82f6) -> Transparent
        // High pressure: Dark Blue (#0f172a) -> Black (#000000)
        
        const r = 15 - (pressure * 15);
        const g = 23 - (pressure * 23);
        const b = 42 - (pressure * 42);
        
        const grad = ctx.createLinearGradient(0, 0, w, 0);
        grad.addColorStop(0, `rgba(${r}, ${g}, ${b}, 1)`); // Left side (Ship area)
        grad.addColorStop(1, '#020617'); // Right side (Deep space/TSC)
        
        ctx.fillStyle = grad;
        ctx.fillRect(0, 0, w, h);

        // 2. Stars with Motion Blur
        ctx.fillStyle = '#ffffff';
        stars.forEach(star => {
          // Move stars left based on velocity
          star.x -= star.speed * (velocity * 2);
          if (star.x < 0) star.x += w;

          // Draw streak if moving fast
          if (velocity > 1) {
            ctx.globalAlpha = 0.5;
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(star.x, star.y);
            ctx.lineTo(star.x + (velocity * 10), star.y);
            ctx.strokeStyle = '#fff';
            ctx.lineWidth = star.size / 2;
            ctx.stroke();
            ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;
          } else {
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.arc(star.x, star.y, star.size, 0, Math.PI*2);
            ctx.fill();
          }
        });

        // 3. The Ship (Fixed Position)
        const shipX = 100;
        const shipY = h / 2;
        
        // Ship Body
        ctx.fillStyle = '#e2e8f0';
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(shipX, shipY);
        ctx.lineTo(shipX - 20, shipY - 10);
        ctx.lineTo(shipX - 20, shipY + 10);
        ctx.fill();
        
        // Engine Glow (only when pushing)
        if ((mode === 'standard' && energy > 0) || (mode === 'pulse' && distance % 400 < 200 && energy > 0)) {
           ctx.fillStyle = '#f59e0b';
           ctx.beginPath();
           ctx.moveTo(shipX - 20, shipY - 5);
           ctx.lineTo(shipX - 35 - (velocity*2), shipY);
           ctx.lineTo(shipX - 20, shipY + 5);
           ctx.fill();
        }

        // 4. Light Speed Barrier (The Black Bar)
        ctx.fillStyle = '#000000';
        ctx.fillRect(BARRIER_POS, 0, 20, h);
        
        ctx.fillStyle = '#ef4444';
        ctx.font = 'bold 12px sans-serif';
        ctx.fillText('LIGHT SPEED BARRIER', BARRIER_POS - 60, 30);
        ctx.fillText('(TSC Boundary)', BARRIER_POS - 60, 50);

        // 5. UI Bars
        // Pressure Bar
        ctx.fillStyle = '#1e293b';
        ctx.fillRect(20, h - 60, w - 40, 10);
        ctx.fillStyle = pressure > 0.8 ? '#ef4444' : '#3b82f6';
        ctx.fillRect(20, h - 60, (w - 40) * pressure, 10);
        ctx.fillStyle = '#94a3b8';
        ctx.font = '10px sans-serif';
        ctx.fillText('TEMPORAL PRESSURE (Drag)', 20, h - 65);

        // Energy Bar
        ctx.fillStyle = '#1e293b';
        ctx.fillRect(20, h - 30, w - 40, 10);
        ctx.fillStyle = energy > 30 ? '#10b981' : '#ef4444';
        ctx.fillRect(20, h - 30, (w - 40) * (energy / 100), 10);
        ctx.fillText('SHIP ENERGY', 20, h - 35);
      }

      function update() {
        const w = canvas.logicalWidth || 800;
        
        if (mode === 'standard') {
          // Standard: Continuous push, pressure builds, energy drains
          if (energy > 0 && velocity < MAX_SPEED * 0.9) {
             velocity += 0.05;
             energy -= 0.3;
             pressure += 0.01; // Pressure builds up
             if (pressure > 1) pressure = 1;
             statusText.innerText = "Standard Drive: Pressure building. Energy draining rapidly.";
             statusText.style.color = "#ef4444";
          } else {
             if (energy <= 0) {
                velocity *= 0.98; // Slow down
                pressure *= 0.95; // Pressure releases
                statusText.innerText = "Standard Drive: Fuel depleted. Drifting.";
             }
          }
        } 
        else if (mode === 'pulse') {
          // Pulse Logic
          let cyclePos = distance % 400;
          
          if (cyclePos < 200 && energy > 0 && velocity < MAX_SPEED * 0.95) {
             // Push Phase
             velocity += 0.08;
             energy -= 0.15;
             pressure += 0.02;
             if (pressure > 1) pressure = 1;
             statusText.innerText = "Pulse Drive: Accelerating. Temporal pressure increasing.";
             statusText.style.color = "#f59e0b";
          } else {
             // Coast Phase
             pressure *= 0.92; // Pressure releases quickly
             if (pressure < 0.05) pressure = 0;
             
             // Maintain momentum (Newton's 1st Law)
             velocity *= 0.999; 
             
             // Small energy drain for systems
             if (energy > 0) energy -= 0.05;
             
             statusText.innerText = "Pulse Drive: Coasting. Pressure dissipated. Momentum maintained.";
             statusText.style.color = "#3b82f6";
          }
          distance += velocity;
        }

        // Cap velocity at barrier approach
        if (velocity > MAX_SPEED * 0.98) {
           velocity = MAX_SPEED * 0.98;
           statusText.innerText = "WARNING: Approaching TSC Boundary. Infinite energy required to cross.";
           statusText.style.color = "#ef4444";
        }

        draw();
        if (mode !== 'none' || velocity > 0.1) {
          animationId = requestAnimationFrame(update);
        }
      }

      btnStandard.addEventListener('click', () => {
        reset();
        mode = 'standard';
        update();
      });

      btnPulse.addEventListener('click', () => {
        reset();
        mode = 'pulse';
        update();
      });

      btnReset.addEventListener('click', reset);

      function reset() {
        mode = 'none';
        velocity = 0;
        pressure = 0;
        energy = 100;
        distance = 0;
        statusText.innerText = "Select a drive mode.";
        statusText.style.color = "#94a3b8";
        draw();
        cancelAnimationFrame(animationId);
      }

      window.addEventListener('resize', resizeCanvas);
      resizeCanvas();
      draw();
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>